348	     * Enforces the pre-persistence policies that reject a newly mapped and normalized owner
349	     * outright, in order, before any derived fields are assigned or the owner is saved. Each
350	     * independent rule lives in its own {@code rejectWhen...} guard and is applied here in order, so
351	     * the sequence of create-time rejections stays readable and a new rule is added as one more
352	     * guard. Grouping the rules here keeps {@link #addOwner} focused on the household, derived-field
353	     * and persistence steps. The single duplicate rule that rejects an owner whose whole identity
354	     * key matches an existing one is applied separately in {@link #rejectWhenIdentityInUse}.
355	     *
